    "logic": {
      "concept": "Two Bollinger envelopes around one SMA(20). A move that clears 0.5 SD from its own 20-bar mean has stopped being noise around that mean and started being a direction; the participants who must react to it - stops, hedges, mandates - are the edge. The neutral zone inside +/-0.5 SD is where the mean still explains the tape and nothing is traded. Trades are attributed by their ENTRY bar, never the exit, so a breakout opened in one quadrant that runs into another still scores where it opened.",
      "entry": "LONG when Close crosses ABOVE SMA(20) + 0.5 x SD, entering the buy zone. SHORT when Close crosses BELOW SMA(20) - 0.5 x SD. With use_outer_guard the zone is BOUNDED at 3.0 SD and a close beyond it is treated as overextended rather than as a signal.",
      "exit": "Price returning to the neutral zone (back inside +/-0.5 SD), or Close crossing back through the SMA(20) baseline with use_baseline_exit - whichever the bar reaches first. A protective stop at 1.5 x ATR(14) sits underneath both. No take-profit is modelled (tp_atr_mult=None) and the engine's ATR trail is off (trailing=False): the SMA is the trailing exit here, and it is a SIGNAL rather than a bracket."
    }
  },
